DESCRIPTION:Wednesday\, April 1\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Moti
 on Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 49m\n\n1960 | 109 min. | USA | Black-and-White 
 | English | Rated R \nDIRECTED BY: Alfred Hitchcock  \nWRITTEN BY: Joseph
  Stefano\nWITH: Anthony Perkins\, Vera Miles\, John Gavin\, Janet Leigh\n\
 nType: Screenings\n\n“When I was a kid\,” director Bong Joon Ho writes
  in the catalog for his current exhibition at the Academy Museum\, “I wa
 tched so many Alfred Hitchcock movies on Korean television. Hitchcock is s
 till one of my biggest inspirations. I’ve seen Psycho more than 50 times
 .” This psychological thriller opens with Marion Crane (Janet Leigh) abs
 conding with $40\,000 cash from her employer in Phoenix to deliver to her 
 debt-ridden fiancé in California. Along the way she stops at the Bates Mo
 tel\, where an encounter with curious innkeeper Norman (Anthony Perkins) b
 egets one of the most harrowing and famous scenes in cinema history. An It
 alian poster from Bong’s personal collection hangs in the exhibition\, o
 n view on Level 2\, and he included the title on his 2022 Sight & Sound li
 st as one of 10 films that he considers the greatest of all time.
