 he Housemaid was restored in 2008 by the Korean Film Archive (KOFA)\, in a
 ssociation with The Film Foundation’s World Cinema Project and HFR-Digit
 al Film laboratory. Additional restoration funded by Armani\, Cartier\, Qa
 tar Airways\, and Qatar Museum Authority.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nRadical a
 nd uncompromising\, Kim Ki-young’s Housemaid trilogy starts in 1960 with
  a first chapter that continues to influence new generations of filmmakers
  more than 60 years later. A deep survey on desire\, obsession\, and ego-d
 riven revenge\, this domestic horror film follows a bourgeois family who h
 ires Myung-sook (Lee Eun-shim)\, an unsophisticated young woman\, as their
  housemaid. When she becomes smitten with patriarch Dong-sik Kim\, a serie
 s of strange episodes unfold\, and Myung-sook’s catastrophic infatuation
