BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Stray Dog (Nora inu) in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260410
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260411
DTSTAMP:20260329T015426Z
UID:019c0634-e877-2a82-3436-1d52e10104d4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, April 10\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion
  Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 2m\n\n1949 | 122 min. | Japan | Black-and-White |
  Japanese with English subtitles | Not Rated | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Akira K
 urosawa \nWRITTEN BY: Ryuzo Kikushima\, Akira Kurosawa \nWITH: Toshiro Mif
 une\, Takashi Shimura\, Keiko Awaji\, Eiko Miyoshi\n\nType: Screenings\n\n
 Rookie detective Murakami (Toshiro Mifune) loses his pistol to a pickpocke
 t in a crowded\, sweltering streetcar during his first day on the job. To 
 save face\, and with the help of skilled detective Sato (Takashi Shimura)\
 , he goes undercover through Tokyo’s underground to capture the culprit 
 before any crimes are committed. An early breakthrough in Kurosawa’s car
 eer\, Stray Dog explores the desperation of postwar Japanese society. Isao
  Kimura’s portrayal of the disillusioned war veteran-turned-thief marked
  the actor’s first appearance in a Kurosawa film.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/calendar/stray-dog-in-35-mm-019c0634-
 e877-2a82-3436-1d52e10104d4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zodiac with David Fincher and Bong Joon Ho
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260411
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260412
DTSTAMP:20260329T015426Z
UID:019c7ce1-27ac-6b1c-34b6-7442623ce54d@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, April 11\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Moti
 on Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 37m\n\n2007 | 157 min. | USA | English | Color 
 | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: David Fincher \nWRITTEN BY: James Vanderbil
 t \nWITH: Jake Gyllenhaal\, Robert Downey Jr.\, Mark Ruffalo\, Anthony Edw
 ards\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector David Fincher’s 2007 thriller excav
 ates a notorious series of real unsolved murders that petrified the San Fr
 ancisco Bay Area in the late 1960s. Jake Gyllenhaal portrays Robert Graysm
 ith\, a cartoonist whose amateur investigation into the serial killer\, kn
 own only as Zodiac\, complements the efforts of SFPD inspector Dave Toschi
  (Mark Ruffalo) and San Francisco Chronicle reporter Paul Avery (Robert Do
 wney Jr.). \nFincher’s dense narrative offers various interpretations of
  the crimes and Zodiac’s identity\, avoiding the cliché channelings typ
 ical of crime thrillers. An original poster from the film is on view in th
 e current exhibition Director’s Inspiration: Bong Joon Ho.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/calendar/zodiac-019c7ce1-27ac-6b1c-34
 b6-7442623ce54d
END:VEVENT
