BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gallery Spotlight: Shaping Hollywoodland
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260529T133000
DTSTAMP:20260329T015426Z
UID:019a0315-24e2-4f88-59de-e64d5b51f067@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, May 29\, 2026 at Noon–1pm\n\nLocation: Spielberg Fa
 mily Gallery\n\nType: Conversations\n\nHollywoodland: Jewish Founders and 
 the Making of a Movie Capital explores the impact of the predominantly Jew
 ish filmmakers who played a key role in establishing the American film stu
 dio system\, transforming Los Angeles into a global epicenter of cinema. \
 nBeth Kean\, CEO of Holocaust Museum LA\, and Warren Sherk\, director of s
 pecial collections of the Margaret Herrick Library\, discuss the museum’
 s first permanent exhibition\, highlighting new objects that showcase nota
 ble Oscar wins and the origins of motion picture history. \nModerated by R
 achel Rosenfeld\, associate director\, Academy Collections Acquisitions.\n
 About Gallery SpotlightsGallery Spotlights feature special guests who brin
 g fresh insights to our exhibitions. Join us for revealing monthly convers
 ations connecting the objects in our galleries to the art and history of m
 oviemaking.\nIf you have any questions or need assistance planning your vi
 sit\, please email museumeducation@oscars.org.
LOCATION:Spielberg Family Gallery
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/calendar/gallery-spotlight-shaping-ho
 llywoodland-019a0315-24e2-4f88-59de-e64d5b51f067
END:VEVENT
